{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox","id":1152337,"title":"How \"Harry Potter\" can you get without throwing out Paradox?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-23T17:22:22-07:00","id":1152337,"title":"How \"Harry Potter\" can you get without throwing out Paradox?","content":"Was wonder while watching a recent Harry Potter Esque movie &quot;Fantastic Creatures&quot; or some such how close you can get to that kind of fantasy using mage.<br /> <br /> since in mage &quot;Paradox&quot; puts a definite surcharge on anything fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T17:46:07-07:00","id":1152344,"title":"","content":"Well, how long an intervallum are we speaking about and are you very attached to that character? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:04:23-07:00","id":1152374,"title":"","content":"Like PM\u00e1rk suggests, you can get pretty blatant with magic for a little while, but eventually Paradox will catch up to you. As with Harry Potter, the biggest constraint against using obvious magic out in the open is that normal people knowing about magic is bad for those who use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:14:11-07:00","id":1152377,"title":"","content":"Paradox is an issue in the Mundane world. Mage has both access to all sorts of hidden places via reality Zone, Multiple Spirit planes, Realms to interact with etc. You can get very Harry Potter as long as you are in secret places. A reality zone that works like Hogworts, doors to the Hollow Earth or some bygone's realm. The big thing is the weird and fantastical is not a thing in that can happen in public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:26:14-07:00","id":1152380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152377#post1152377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is an issue in the Mundane world. Mage has both access to all sorts of hidden places via reality Zone, Multiple Spirit planes, Realms to interact with etc. You can get very Harry Potter as long as you are in secret places. A reality zone that works like Hogworts, doors to the Hollow Earth or some bygone's realm. The big thing is the weird and fantastical is not a thing in that can happen in public.</div> </div> </div> </div>That too. It depends on the timeline in question, but in the Umbra, Horizon realms, Chantries, fitting reality zones and such, you could really bring out the fireworks, as well as against other nightfolks. Under Revised, it's more problematic, because most of those realms were cut off and Paradox rules were harsher, but still. In M20, under the right situations, you could go bonkers, just not totally bonkers. Given, it could still blow up in your face, but hey, it's Mage, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, yeah, I agree, it's quite Harry Potter-esque in that regard. As it came up in another thread, I really can't visualize, for example, the fall of Horizon without all kind of CGI, dragons battling umbraships and everyone tossing around all kinds of blatant reality warping as if there would be no tomorrow (since there wasn't...).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 10-23-2017, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T02:53:32-07:00","id":1152442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox#post1152337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was wonder while watching a recent Harry Potter Esque movie &quot;Fantastic Creatures&quot; or some such how close you can get to that kind of fantasy using mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't get close at all. Mage: The Ascension is a different and more sensible envisioning of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T06:11:23-07:00","id":1152479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152442#post1152442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't get close at all. Mage: The Ascension is a different and more sensible envisioning of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough RAW, a Mage Academy, would have little actual magic, mostly memorizing theoretical i ncantations, or effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T06:26:26-07:00","id":1152482,"title":"","content":"If you're willing to do some far-out HAP-based adjudication of Paradox, you can get pretty damn close.<br /> <br /> The main difference between Mage and Harry Potter is that in Harry Potter, Muggles aren't supposed to know about magic - so it needs to be out of sight or otherwise concealed. If there's a Muggle on the other side of a layer of drywall, you can pretty much go nuts. In Mage, you aren't supposed to diverge from the local Consensus - so in a sense, you're always being observed by Muggles, just sometimes more so as they actually look at you. <br /> <br /> Hypothetical Average Perceiver says that a spell is vulgar if an average perceiver - like a person standing in front of you - would see what you're doing and say, &quot;That's impossible!&quot; Thus you don't materialize a revolver in your hand, you materialize it in your pocket and pull it out. Now your spell is coincidental rather than vulgar-with-witnesses.<br /> <br /> If you decide that there is no &quot;vulgar-without-witnesses&quot; category - that a Sleeper has to actually witness your magic in some way to make it vulgar - then you're pretty much in Harry Potter territory, and you can do all sorts of cool stuff on the other side of that drywall. You should still take into account non-visual witnessing (say, creating an earthquake powerful enough to register on Sleeper seismographs would be &quot;witnessed&quot;).<br /> <br /> For your specific example of Fantastic Beasts - they get pretty freewheeling towards the end, with folks walking around throwing repair charms at basically the entire city. I think that's playing pretty loose with Harry Potter-level magic secrecy, and it would certainly not get past the model I proposed above. I personally think that's a feature rather than a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T07:56:17-07:00","id":1152506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152482#post1152482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For your specific example of Fantastic Beasts - they get pretty freewheeling towards the end, with folks walking around throwing repair charms at basically the entire city. I think that's playing pretty loose with Harry Potter-level magic secrecy, and it would certainly not get past the model I proposed above. I personally think that's a feature rather than a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeell, they did some pretty big stuff during the Quidditch World Cup in the 4th book. Maybe Americans were just less conservative, especially that in the era of fantastic beasts even photography cameras weren't something everybody had.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from that, magic in HP, if you really think about it, is pretty darn powerfull, with very little constraints. As long as they have their instruments, they can go on and on and on, throwing around high-level effects, far above what spellcasters in most rpgs are capable of (but they don't have the really-really high end effects). Unlimited teleportation at the age of 17 as a widespread thing???? In a sense, that's more close to Mage than to D&amp;D, or a manapoint-based system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T08:31:10-07:00","id":1152516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152506#post1152506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unlimited teleportation at the age of 17 as a widespread thing???? In a sense, that's more close to Mage than to D&amp;D, or a manapoint-based system.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can actually screw up the teleportation and end up hurt... although it is somewhat inconsistent. In one book a character leaves her leg behind and nothing gory happens while in the last book Ron almost bleeds to death from a fail teleportation.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was the distance...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T08:42:42-07:00","id":1152517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrakeEpsilon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152516#post1152516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can actually screw up the teleportation and end up hurt... although it is somewhat inconsistent. In one book a character leaves her leg behind and nothing gory happens while in the last book Ron almost bleeds to death from a fail teleportation.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was the distance...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe, but it's essentially on the same level as getting a driving license for muggles. <br /> <br /> Also, changing things' size, without time limits or any concern about conservation of matter? Casual use of mass-level space-warping? Transformation between living things and non-living, taught in school to teenagers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T09:02:53-07:00","id":1152526,"title":"","content":"Hmmh.<br /> <br /> Actually, I wonder. If you'd see Hogwarts as a school of Sorcerors instead of full blown Mages, a few things click into place. The spellbook-like nature of the spells basically equaling path rituals, the lack of paradox behind the aformentioned drywall, the repeatable hermetic structure of the teaching.<br /> <br /> I think that could work quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T09:51:28-07:00","id":1152537,"title":"","content":"OK, going to try to toe a line here, but have you considered looking at Mage: the Awakening 2e?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying go full CofD if you want something more HP, but the Awakening 2e spell system is exceedingly easier to mesh with the Potterverse than Ascension's is, and the general social setup is easier to do as well.<br /> <br /> A lot of this comes down to the differences in the two games. While Ascension, Awakening, and the Potterverse all strong ground their conflicts in battles between mages, each other, and the Sleepers/muggles around them, Ascension's focus is much more on &quot;What is magic?&quot; while Awakening and the Potterverse both focus more on, &quot;What do I do with magic?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:11:10-07:00","id":1152609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152526#post1152526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmh.<br /> <br /> Actually, I wonder. If you'd see Hogwarts as a school of Sorcerors instead of full blown Mages, a few things click into place. The spellbook-like nature of the spells basically equaling path rituals, the lack of paradox behind the aformentioned drywall, the repeatable hermetic structure of the teaching.<br /> <br /> I think that could work quite well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially if you consider the notion I always had that probably, basically most adult wizards and witches in HP are just doing stuff in a very unrestrained and freeway mode (I always felt that, for example, Dumbledore just doesn't care about the -otherwise very loosely- established in-universe rules of dong magic). Not just Wordless, but more like &quot;I want to do this, so THIS will happen&quot;. It could be a Hermetic Chantry-school, where mages are teaching kids Hermetic Sorcery with the goal of awakening them. The majority won't but they'll become good sorcererers, but the really good ones Awaken and later become teachers themselves, prominent members of society, or sociopathic dark wizards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T20:53:48-07:00","id":1152691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152482#post1152482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main difference between Mage and Harry Potter is that in Harry Potter, Muggles aren't supposed to know about magic - so it needs to be out of sight or otherwise concealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mage: the Ascension mundane humans are not to know about True Magick as well, to an extent. There is of course the idea of showing it to them, but the secrecy that True Mages do keep is more important, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T21:05:01-07:00","id":1152696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152526#post1152526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmh.<br /> <br /> Actually, I wonder. If you'd see Hogwarts as a school of Sorcerors instead of full blown Mages, a few things click into place. The spellbook-like nature of the spells basically equaling path rituals, the lack of paradox behind the aformentioned drywall, the repeatable hermetic structure of the teaching.<br /> <br /> I think that could work quite well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with the idea hogwarts should be a sorcerer academy, but think broadly to get a full wizarding world its going to need judicious use of 2e Horizon realms and Reality zones.<br /> <br /> If you want magical beasts to be more &quot;available&quot; than secret places in other worlds or the most hidden places on earth. Well changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T09:43:10-07:00","id":1152834,"title":"","content":"You could just ditch Paradox and the concepts of Coincidental vs. Vulgar, Sleepers vs. No Sleepers on Difficulties. Then just make doing magic in front of Sleepers a VERY bad idea socially. Sorta the same way that Vampires don't go &quot;Poof&quot; if mortals see them use Disciplines but allowing that to happen will end up getting you punished if anyone finds out about it. If every time a mage was reported for doing magic in front of Sleepers there was an effing Tribunal convened to try him or her Star Chamber style and excuses like &quot;but if I didn't do I would have died&quot; carry some, but not a lot of weight.... Well, it's a different game but not really all that different. It's just taking out the mechanics of making magic hurt through roll-playing and making them happen because of role-playing. <br /> <br /> Hells, maybe you DO keep some issues of Diff. in play based on Coincidental vs. Vulgar, but invert them. Doing Coincidental magic is MORE difficult but it means that the Sleepers are going to be shaking their heads and wondering why something so wacky happened (and your character doesn't go to jail) while Vulgar magic is doing something closer to the true nature of magic and, therefore, actually easier. Oh, and without having to track the Paradox Pool, you've simplified things quite substantially. And botches just become botches instead of a gateway into a labyrinth of varying effects based on math and situation and, then, ultimately, fiat. Instead of going straight to the botches are handled by ST fiat that goes for pretty much every other game and every other circumstance using the WW game engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T12:13:25-07:00","id":1152866,"title":"","content":"This is one of the reasons I'd suggest at least looking at how Awakening 2e handles things if you want to go that sort of route. It ditches Coincidental vs. Vulgar, witnesses only count for obvious magic and have a very small impact regardless, the Paradox system isn't less complex but is always resolved per spell rather than building up with points and there's a lot less fiat involved (plus more player choice), and there's quite a large number of consequences that are more external to the mage to use as social consequence fodder (ex: it's really not hard to avoid significant Paradox while casting a bit fancy effect in front of a lot of Sleepers, but you can't really do anything about the fact that you caused significant psychological harm to a sizeable portion of them... which other mages aren't going to like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:05:19-07:00","id":1152888,"title":"","content":"I agree that Awakening would be something of a better fit, but the fit is going to be...askew if you are genuinely looking to get away with something similar to the Potteverse. The Awakening Paradox consequences are somewhat quirky and often a little off-kilter to the effects that generate them and they definitely don't give the same &quot;feel&quot; because, even when they don't match up to the conceit of the setting, that of the Fallen World and the Lie that humans partake of and in, they do come from that place. Which is a very different place. Maybe the Awakening rules in general with some skew on the Paradox effects....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:09:15-07:00","id":1152967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152834#post1152834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just ditch Paradox and the concepts of Coincidental vs. Vulgar, Sleepers vs. No Sleepers on Difficulties. Then just make doing magic in front of Sleepers a VERY bad idea socially. Sorta the same way that Vampires don't go &quot;Poof&quot; if mortals see them use Disciplines but allowing that to happen will end up getting you punished if anyone finds out about it. If every time a mage was reported for doing magic in front of Sleepers there was an effing Tribunal convened to try him or her Star Chamber style and excuses like &quot;but if I didn't do I would have died&quot; carry some, but not a lot of weight.... Well, it's a different game but not really all that different. It's just taking out the mechanics of making magic hurt through roll-playing and making them happen because of role-playing.<br /> <br /> Hells, maybe you DO keep some issues of Diff. in play based on Coincidental vs. Vulgar, but invert them. Doing Coincidental magic is MORE difficult but it means that the Sleepers are going to be shaking their heads and wondering why something so wacky happened (and your character doesn't go to jail) while Vulgar magic is doing something closer to the true nature of magic and, therefore, actually easier. Oh, and without having to track the Paradox Pool, you've simplified things quite substantially. And botches just become botches instead of a gateway into a labyrinth of varying effects based on math and situation and, then, ultimately, fiat. Instead of going straight to the botches are handled by ST fiat that goes for pretty much every other game and every other circumstance using the WW game engine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd like a game like that a lot, as <i>another </i>modern, magic and magician-centered rpg! It's more like Dresden and not really fitting for Ascension's themes, but it's good.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote, I can't really understand why there isn't any official rpgs set in the Potterwerse. The setting just have soooo much potential and instead it's just constrained for what JKR writes and the occasional film and Pottermore. Legendary Beasts showed the possibilities of alternative stories and characters, even timelines, set in the same universe, so there's hope, maybe we'll have something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:14:54-07:00","id":1152971,"title":"","content":"You can get ludicrously vulgar... Until you run out of Quint to pay the bills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T18:03:21-07:00","id":1152992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152967#post1152967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I'd like a game like that a lot, as <i>another </i>modern, magic and magician-centered rpg! It's more like Dresden and not really fitting for Ascension's themes, but it's good.<br /> <br /> As a sidenote, I can't really understand why there isn't any official rpgs set in the Potterwerse. The setting just have soooo much potential and instead it's just constrained for what JKR writes and the occasional film and Pottermore. Legendary Beasts showed the possibilities of alternative stories and characters, even timelines, set in the same universe, so there's hope, maybe we'll have something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> JKR doesn't want to license it. Its really that simple she has control of her property and has no desire for an rpg to exist. Rpgs also don't have the &quot;dump truck full of money&quot; return on investment option that some things do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T18:25:50-07:00","id":1152997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152992#post1152992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> JKR doesn't want to license it. Its really that simple she has control of her property and has no desire for an rpg to exist. Rpgs also don't have the &quot;dump truck full of money&quot; return on investment option that some things do.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;can't really understand&quot; wasn't the best turn of phrase. I get it, I just don't like it. Really, it has so much potential, it's sad from an rpg-fan viewpoint. Also, I'm not really sure JKR is even very aware about rpgs in general, or encountered with them much.<br /> <br /> It's okay for SW to have an rpg. For LotR, for GoT, for Star Trek, Marvel, for a lot of big franchises. It'd be just great to have one in the Potterwerse. There could be even different versions for children adn adults, etc. Yes, it's not the &quot;dump truck full of money&quot;, but it wouldn't harm her, or WB either and it'd be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:22:25-07:00","id":1153007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1152997#post1152997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;can't really understand&quot; wasn't the best turn of phrase. I get it, I just don't like it. Really, it has so much potential, it's sad from an rpg-fan viewpoint. Also, I'm not really sure JKR is even very aware about rpgs in general, or encountered with them much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having had this discussion on multiple sites with people who claimed to have made the attempt. She is on some level actively hostile to the idea of such. Yes it sucks. Yes there are completely horrible licenses that she's signed off on, that's why I bring up the dump truck full of money argument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's okay for SW to have an rpg. For LotR, for GoT, for Star Trek, Marvel, for a lot of big franchises. It'd be just great to have one in the Potterwerse. There could be even different versions for children adn adults, etc. Yes, it's not the &quot;dump truck full of money&quot;, but it wouldn't harm her, or WB either and it'd be nice. </div> </div> </div>Well this has to do with differences of type and the Licence agreements behind each. SW the D6 rpg was intially treated as story bible. Lucas seemed to intially very fond of it sending out the books to the new writers when they started the EU. He has become less over time, thus the SW license has generally come as part of a package for other things(WOTC had it has part of a cardgame setup, FFG has it as part and parcel to their mini game licenses)<br /> <br /> The LOTR rpgs has to do with the Tolkien estate basically losing the rights for relicensing to a conman in the 60s thus why no LOTR rpg ever is able to use stuff from the Similarion or Lost tales(and why we will never get a Simiarlion based movie)<br /> <br /> GRR Martin is pretty RPG friendly so having a GOT game is something he'd actively help vs hinder.<br /> <br /> Star Trek is well compicated, but both Paramount and CBS have a license for it, but both could use some cheap good will drummed up for the Franchise. <br /> <br /> Marvel currently doesn't have a game and hasn't for quite a number of years because of the cost was too high for license renewal.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say the Potterverse doesn't quite match up the situations of the other works. Its selling solidly on other fronts. It doesn't need a kick. JKR doesn't want a game and that's really all there is to it. Though why someone hasn't just done &quot;Modern wizard school&quot; game with the numbers filled off I've never quite understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:34:51-07:00","id":1153012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153007#post1153007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having had this discussion on multiple sites with people who claimed to have made the attempt. She is on some level actively hostile to the idea of such. Yes it sucks. Yes there are completely horrible licenses that she's signed off on, that's why I bring up the dump truck full of money argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's really sad. HP means a lot to me, since childhood, so it's sad to read something like that about JKR. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe she got stuck in the satanic panic thing, given her age and background. Anyway, agree, it sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though why someone hasn't just done &quot;Modern wizard school&quot; game with the numbers filled off I've never quite understood. </div> </div> </div>They did, for example as very big, exclaimed LARP games, in real castles, etc. Not t tabletop,a s far as I'm aware, but surely there's something out there.<br /> <br /> Although, the wizarding school thing, while awesome and takes up the majority of the HP books, is not really the prominent thing I'd want from a hypothetical HP rpg, but more of an &quot;extended universe&quot; kind of thing, like Fantastic Beasts was, because that film and the glimpses of the bigger world in the books were exactly which showed how awesome a full-blown setting it could be, even a quite mature one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:59:30-07:00","id":1153040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153012#post1153012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's really sad. HP means a lot to me, since childhood, so it's sad to read something like that about JKR. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe she got stuck in the satanic panic thing, given her age and background. Anyway, agree, it sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah she just doesn't want other people writing her stuff basically, also she's somewhat familiar with the less savory side of Harry Potter Mush/chat/freeform rpgs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although, the wizarding school thing, while awesome and takes up the majority of the HP books, is not really the prominent thing I'd want from a hypothetical HP rpg, but more of an &quot;extended universe&quot; kind of thing, like Fantastic Beasts was, because that film and the glimpses of the bigger world in the books were exactly which showed how awesome a full-blown setting it could be, even a quite mature one. </div> </div> </div>To bring it back vaguely On topic, the reason I think you need to start with the Wizard School level is so you know how much bigger the Adult graduate should be. To use mage as an example if Starting level Pcs are supposed to be adult wizards it doesn't give much room for School age wizards. Conversely if you had Adepts being the presumed Adult level magic with Masters and archmages being specialists you have more wiggle room.<br /> <br /> So a theoretical HP rpg should start with Kids as playable and how far you want to let that stretch before they run into adult powerscale. Then you can build a post graduate related game once you have a general &quot;this is what everyone can do&quot; scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:03:28-07:00","id":1153494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153040#post1153040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To bring it back vaguely On topic, the reason I think you need to start with the Wizard School level is so you know how much bigger the Adult graduate should be. To use mage as an example if Starting level Pcs are supposed to be adult wizards it doesn't give much room for School age wizards. Conversely if you had Adepts being the presumed Adult level magic with Masters and archmages being specialists you have more wiggle room.<br /> <br /> So a theoretical HP rpg should start with Kids as playable and how far you want to let that stretch before they run into adult powerscale. Then you can build a post graduate related game once you have a general &quot;this is what everyone can do&quot; scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kinda, sorta the topic, which seems to rest on a presumption that one CAN use the Mage RAW to simulate something close enough to Potterverse magic (for which the power progression makes sense - Arete 3 trainees, Arete 4 common adult level of proficiency, Arete 5+ the great mages of the age) except that there are very few examples of anything like the Paradox-riddled nature of Mage magic with every magic wielder acting as an incrementally dangerous time bomb that might explode just 'cause and WILL eventually explode at some point just for doing the kind of Potterverse-style magic this whole thread is about, and, at the very least will be beating themselves up or causing small mishaps all the time....<br /> <br /> Which there actually IS something of in the books. Wands blowing up. People suffering unpleasant, usually silly, side effects from a miscast spell, splinching, etc. But it seems like it's mostly a training issue, which the reverse of Mage magical progression where it is often more and more likely that doing magic is going to get more and more personally dangerous as one advances in power in ability than otherwise. Seamus may have his wand blow up while trying simple levitation spells (Forces 2), but Dumbledore and Voldemort and Newt Scamander can accomplish AWESOME works of magic with no issues at all, often on the fly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T15:02:16-07:00","id":1153595,"title":"","content":"I think you cna get close to Potter magic though not a perfect fit because its well purely narrative with mage with judicious use of Reality zones and Horizon realms. Mages have to play it safe in Mundane reality, but there's many hidden places where things are different. Places where Bygones still dwell and cryptids roam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T19:00:11-07:00","id":1153640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153595#post1153595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you cna get close to Potter magic though not a perfect fit because its well purely narrative with mage with judicious use of Reality zones and Horizon realms. Mages have to play it safe in Mundane reality, but there's many hidden places where things are different. Places where Bygones still dwell and cryptids roam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reality Zones and Horizon Realms, like apparently, New York City and London.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T19:18:50-07:00","id":1153643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153640#post1153640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reality Zones and Horizon Realms, like apparently, New York City and London.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, but particular places in London or New York city where things are wierd, or holes into other worlds would be how to cover a world where there might be such oddities. You obviously can't reach the same places because there are some broad differences. But if you want hidden places where are there are unicorns, schools on mars etc. Those are options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T20:32:34-07:00","id":1153655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153643#post1153643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, but particular places in London or New York city where things are wierd, or holes into other worlds would be how to cover a world where there might be such oddities. You obviously can't reach the same places because there are some broad differences. But if you want hidden places where are there are unicorns, schools on mars etc. Those are options.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's categorically NOT what is going on. Sure there are the hidden parts where they hang out most of the time, but watch the Aurors in Fantastic Beasts. They are categorically NOT hanging out in some house elf run gin joint or MACUSA HQ. They are teleporting like mad, casting charms, raising magical barriers, all in full sight of the nomajs of NYC. And nary a one is incandescing, has their skelelton start glowing, im or explodes, drops into a Paradox Realm, had Wrinkle show up. And that is when the people with most magic are using most of the flashiest possible magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T21:55:53-07:00","id":1153670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153655#post1153655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's categorically NOT what is going on. Sure there are the hidden parts where they hang out most of the time, but watch the Aurors in Fantastic Beasts. They are categorically NOT hanging out in some house elf run gin joint or MACUSA HQ. They are teleporting like mad, casting charms, raising magical barriers, all in full sight of the nomajs of NYC. And nary a one is incandescing, has their skelelton start glowing, im or explodes, drops into a Paradox Realm, had Wrinkle show up. And that is when the people with most magic are using most of the flashiest possible magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's plenty of things Mage can't do because it doesn't want to have &quot;Open magicians can do anything game&quot; The Op asked &quot;how close can you get&quot; well that's the answer You can have magical secret schools on mars, places in the wilderness where unicorns still roam and hidden alleys no Sleeper can see.<br /> <br /> You can't have people blasting away in public or Dragons going all Kaiju on a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T09:20:46-07:00","id":1153751,"title":"","content":"Essentially, Mage is dark urban fantasy. Harry Potter is fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:07:40-07:00","id":1153774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153751#post1153751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, Mage is dark urban fantasy. Harry Potter is fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say Harry Potter is still Urban fantasy, its a broad category. Just that JKR doesn't have to deal with Harry Potter randomly deciding to go throw fireballs at the some muggle who pissed him off because she has complete control over him vs a player character who might need justification for buying into the whole &quot;hidden world&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:07:40-07:00","id":1153775,"title":"","content":"doublepost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:18:45-07:00","id":1153777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153774#post1153774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd say Harry Potter is still Urban fantasy, its a broad category. Just that JKR doesn't have to deal with Harry Potter randomly deciding to go throw fireballs at the some muggle who pissed him off because she has complete control over him vs a player character who might need justification for buying into the whole &quot;hidden world&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeeeeeeeeeell, 'technically' you're right, it fills the &quot;supernatural world hidden behind the normal&quot; checkbox. Legendary beasts was decidedly urban fantasy, IMO, but most of the HP books are so distanced from the mugle world, it's leaning very heavily on the fantasy side, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:45:35-07:00","id":1153780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153774#post1153774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd say Harry Potter is still Urban fantasy, its a broad category. Just that JKR doesn't have to deal with Harry Potter randomly deciding to go throw fireballs at the some muggle who pissed him off because she has complete control over him vs a player character who might need justification for buying into the whole &quot;hidden world&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, somehow, Vampire gets away with having a hidden world with JUST a social injunction against letting normal folks know, without Paradox as a negative incentive or the Veil or the Mists or Delirium as a naked assist. <br /> <br /> If, every time magic is done in front of mundane folks, the PC was hauled up in front of a Star Chamber proceeding where they would suffer censure or branding or imprisonment or whatever, well, there might be a few players who keep throwing fireballs in public... until they end up in magic jail, geased not to do that, etc. You don't NEED to have Witnesses Vulgar magic be something that bites the characters in the ass to make doing magic in front of muggles end up being a VERY BAD thing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T13:03:18-07:00","id":1153784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153670#post1153670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's plenty of things Mage can't do because it doesn't want to have &quot;Open magicians can do anything game&quot; The Op asked &quot;how close can you get&quot; well that's the answer You can have magical secret schools on mars, places in the wilderness where unicorns still roam and hidden alleys no Sleeper can see.<br /> <br /> You can't have people blasting away in public or Dragons going all Kaiju on a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you are adding to what the OP asked with the implicit assumption that they meant, but didn't say, &quot;and keep the Mage RAW&quot;. Which wasn't there, and, in fact, there were several sub-threads discussing what rules to use and possible hacks to make a more Potterverse friendly sort of Mage.<br /> <br /> There is another presumption that Mage doesn't have fights with Dragons/Kaiju/Dragon Kaiju out in the open with mages blasting away, which is pretty much 100% not true even in cannon. There's no problem with that happening in the game using the RAW, but mages are not the ideal combatants, as Paradox is almost certainly going to affect them before Unbelief affects the Baddie (that is, if the Baddie is subject to Unbelief, which it may not be.... like, say, Ravenna). Mages in Mage RAW can blast away in public. <br /> <br /> In the Potterverse, even with secret schools and hidden places both urban and rural,characters blast away in public with witnesses with no problems at all. Particularly no problems with apparent Paradox. Witness the MACUSA Aurors in Fantastic Beasts, who blast away in public while teleporting from roof-top to roof-top or in the middle of the street at busy intersections, followed by casting heavy duty visible wards in front of a crowd without a single face melting or anyone dying of egregious Pattern burn or any weird spirits showing up and spiriting them away to prison dimensions. <br /> <br /> Paradox just isn't a problem. Botching your roll is (splinching, Seamus blowing up his wand, etc.), but not Paradox. So, either Paradox is so intrinsic to Mage that that doing things Pottervese is just impossible,because you just CAN'T handle situations that are front and center in the source material... (But wait!, Wasn't&quot; no Paradox, but still having Botches&quot; how things work in DA? So much for that argument...) Or the rules are malleable enough, that, if you want to do a simple hack you can have the game you want. Along with anything else that isn't a great fit, like, say, getting rid of the Technocracy and, probably, the whole &quot;Science is Magic&quot; thing. (Which is why the ideas floating around about using Awakenings instead of Ascension were in play.... where you COULD be a wizard using tech to do their spells, but it's still using tech as Foci to do magic, not tech IS magic.... )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T15:29:29-07:00","id":1153816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153780#post1153780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, somehow, Vampire gets away with having a hidden world with JUST a social injunction against letting normal folks know, without Paradox as a negative incentive or the Veil or the Mists or Delirium as a naked assist.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And quite afew people have issue with Vampire being realistic about such things(and basically have the Technocracy doing the heavy lifting possibly even the concensus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T16:57:44-07:00","id":1153836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152337-how-harry-potter-can-you-get-without-throwing-out-paradox?p=1153816#post1153816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And quite afew people have issue with Vampire being realistic about such things(and basically have the Technocracy doing the heavy lifting possibly even the concensus)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where realism comes into play in any of these cases. Surely, it's just as &quot;realistic&quot; that immortal bloodsuckers can keep their existence hidden from a population who are mostly in complete denial and kept utterly distracted as it is that there are such things as immortal bloodsuckers.<br /> <br /> The issue isn't whether it's &quot;realistic&quot;, it's whether it's internally consistent. Paradox doesn't do any better keeping people from seeing magic and having that fuel their belief in it, it just blows up the people that do it. That's doesn't generate disbelief, it generates fear of magical suicide bombers. Paradox doesn't do anything to make magic look less magical or assert some kind of normalcy, it just punishes people for messing up and for doing too much magic without trying to keep their casting and the resulting effects on the downlow. <br /> <br /> So, that being the case, is it pretty much the Rule of Shade and the Pogrom that are keeping magic undercover, not Paradox? Perhaps the primary problem isn't how magic is being kept secret (since it's going to be implausible no matter what), but that the way Paradox works as &quot;magic going wrong&quot; doesn't mirror the way &quot;magic goes wrong&quot; in the Potterverse (where it's a lot more like normal Botching). Again, along with the lack of the &quot;science is magic&quot; and the existence of the Union and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}